comment-226852619"},"message":"In this case, I strongly propose an amendment. I want to keep the pictures on the website, despite the fact that the founding fathers didn't put that explicitly in the proposal.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1466193288,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyNjg2NjQxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/567#issuecomment-226866412"},"message":";-)  And I \"slept on it\", and decided that whatever we would \"publish\" should be really concerned only with presentation/exploration of the datasets.  It should just be pluggable easily into main (lab, consortium, etc) websites either through an ugly subframe or some other, more contemporary technique.  So, in general I do not oppose any face lifting to the main website.  BUT I wonder if it shouldn't be fully sphinx produced?  I find myself quite lost often among multitude of \"faces\" of projects' websites.  As we already know we could do everything, including blog pots etc, with sphinx.  And then later we would just embed the \"datasets.datalad.org\" component into it.","files":null}]}